# Principled BSDF: use the v2 socket names

Blender 4.0 rewrote the Principled BSDF ("Principled v2") and renamed most of
its inputs. Every version this pack supports (4.5 LTS, 5.1, 5.2) uses the new
names, so code from 3.x tutorials and models fails at the first lookup:

```text
KeyError: 'bpy_prop_collection[key]: key "Emission" not found'
```

Measured on 4.5.14 and 5.2.1:

| 3.x input | 4.0+ input |
| --- | --- |
| `Emission` | `Emission Color` (with `Emission Strength`) |
| `Specular` | `Specular IOR Level` |
| `Clearcoat`, `Clearcoat Roughness`, `Clearcoat Normal` | `Coat Weight`, `Coat Roughness`, `Coat Normal` |
| `Subsurface` | `Subsurface Weight` |
| `Subsurface Color` | removed: subsurface takes `Base Color` |
| `Transmission` | `Transmission Weight` |
| `Transmission Roughness` | removed: transmission uses `Roughness` |
| `Sheen` | `Sheen Weight` |
| `Specular Tint`, `Sheen Tint` | same names, now colors (`RGBA`), not floats |

## What this rule flags

- `bsdf.inputs["<3.x name>"]` for any left-column name above, on a
  `ShaderNodeBsdfPrincipled` node
- `bsdf.inputs[<int>]`: the input order moved with v2 and moves again as
  inputs are added (5.2 adds `Thin Wall`), so an index silently names a
  different socket
- A float written to `Specular Tint` or `Sheen Tint`
- A `try`/`except KeyError` fallback to the old name: on supported versions
  the old branch never runs

## Wrong

```python
bsdf = mat.node_tree.nodes["Principled BSDF"]
bsdf.inputs["Emission"].default_value = (1.0, 0.5, 0.1, 1.0)
bsdf.inputs["Specular"].default_value = 0.0
bsdf.inputs["Clearcoat"].default_value = 1.0
bsdf.inputs[17].default_value = 3.0  # meant Emission Strength
```

## Right

```python
bsdf = mat.node_tree.nodes["Principled BSDF"]
bsdf.inputs["Emission Color"].default_value = (1.0, 0.5, 0.1, 1.0)
bsdf.inputs["Emission Strength"].default_value = 3.0
bsdf.inputs["Specular IOR Level"].default_value = 0.0
bsdf.inputs["Coat Weight"].default_value = 1.0
if "Thin Wall" in bsdf.inputs:  # 5.2+ only
    bsdf.inputs["Thin Wall"].default_value = True
```

Look a socket up by name, and guard with `in bsdf.inputs` only for a socket
that is missing on a version you target.

## Verified

`examples/swatch-grid/` sets `Specular IOR Level` on 4.5 and 5.x, and its
`--no-specular-shim` falsifier exits 7 when the name does not resolve. The
3.x-to-4.0 table above was measured on 4.5.14 and 5.2.1 (procedural-materials-
and-shaders skill).

